<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:00:40 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>心爱的河马菲奥娜在吞下不小心扔进动物园围栏的孩子帽子后死亡</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-child-tossed-a-hat-and-a-ceiling-fan-sent-it-flying-into-a-hippos-zoo-enclosure-where-the-animal-ate-it-heres-how-the-care-team-is-responding-180989894/</link><description>动物护理团队最初乐观地认为辛辛那提动物园的网红河马能够自然排出物体并康复，但情况最终变成了“医疗紧急情况”</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:21:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-child-tossed-a-hat-and-a-ceiling-fan-sent-it-flying-into-a-hippos-zoo-enclosure-where-the-animal-ate-it-heres-how-the-care-team-is-responding-180989894/</guid></item><item><title>哈佛归还两个可能属于被奴役者的头骨，150 多年前，这些头骨是从巴西运来用于优生学研究的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/harvard-returns-two-skulls-likely-belonging-to-enslaved-individuals-more-than-150-years-after-they-were-taken-from-brazil-for-eugenics-studies-180989910/</link><description>在研究人员、社区团体和巴西政府多年的压力下，遗骸在里约热内卢和萨尔瓦多举行了隆重的仪式欢迎归来。一个头骨可能属于一位在 1835 年奴隶起义中战斗并死亡的人</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:22:56 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/harvard-returns-two-skulls-likely-belonging-to-enslaved-individuals-more-than-150-years-after-they-were-taken-from-brazil-for-eugenics-studies-180989910/</guid></item><item><title>观看在英格兰切斯特动物园出生的稀有小犀牛，这是对其脆弱物种的可爱促进</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-rare-baby-rhinoceros-born-in-englands-chester-zoo-an-adorable-addition-to-its-species-numbers-180989902/</link><description>这头小牛出生于 10 月 11 日，健康状况良好，正在与母亲一起探索一个僻静的围场，远离公众视线</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:18:05 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-rare-baby-rhinoceros-born-in-englands-chester-zoo-an-adorable-addition-to-its-species-numbers-180989902/</guid></item><item><title>美国国立卫生研究院决定明年将最后一批退休研究黑猩猩转移到动物保护区</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-nih-has-decided-to-move-its-last-group-of-retired-research-chimpanzees-to-an-animal-sanctuary-next-year-180989907/</link><description>该机构此前已确定这些动物年龄太大或患病，不适合此次旅行。但最近涉及另一个联邦政府支持的研究机构的转移促使美国国立卫生研究院重新审视这个问题</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:35:25 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-nih-has-decided-to-move-its-last-group-of-retired-research-chimpanzees-to-an-animal-sanctuary-next-year-180989907/</guid></item><item><title>考古学家最终拼凑出古希腊最大的谜团之一“帕台农神庙之谜”吗？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/have-archaeologists-finally-pieced-together-the-parthenon-puzzle-one-of-ancient-greece-greatest-mysteries-180989903/</link><description>几个世纪前，帕特农神庙的东山墙已化为废墟。德国研究人员现在相信，在罗马石棺和 3D 打印机的帮助下，他们已经重现了描绘雅典娜诞生的 39 幅人物场景</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:06:45 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/have-archaeologists-finally-pieced-together-the-parthenon-puzzle-one-of-ancient-greece-greatest-mysteries-180989903/</guid></item><item><title>这款自动充电牙刷的刷毛可以发电，帮助杀死导致蛀牙和牙龈疾病的细菌</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-self-charging-toothbrush-has-bristles-that-generate-electricity-to-help-kill-bacteria-that-cause-cavities-and-gum-disease-180989895/</link><description>在一项简短的临床试验中，使用实验牙刷的参与者报告说，与使用传统尼龙毛刷的参与者相比，牙菌斑、牙龈炎症和出血更少。然而，需要更多的研究来评估该工具的安全性和有效性</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-self-charging-toothbrush-has-bristles-that-generate-electricity-to-help-kill-bacteria-that-cause-cavities-and-gum-disease-180989895/</guid></item><item><title>这位哲学家是第一批将自己的遗体捐献给科学的人之一。近 200 年后，研究人员仍在从中学习</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/he-was-one-of-the-first-people-to-donate-his-body-to-science-nearly-200-years-later-researchers-are-still-learning-from-it-180989901/</link><description>功利主义创始人杰里米·边沁 (Jeremy Bentham) 的尸体被公开解剖，并变成了一个“自动图标”，这是一个栩栩如生的展示，展示了他穿着一套西装的骷髅</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:31:07 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/he-was-one-of-the-first-people-to-donate-his-body-to-science-nearly-200-years-later-researchers-are-still-learning-from-it-180989901/</guid></item><item><title>北大西洋露脊鲸数量锐减，引发人们对这一极度濒危物种未来的担忧</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-north-atlantic-right-whale-population-has-shrunk-raising-concerns-about-the-future-of-the-critically-endangered-species-180989896/</link><description>大型海洋哺乳动物因船只撞击、渔具缠结和其他原因而死亡，这影响了该物种数量增长的能力。大约100年前，这些动物被猎杀至濒临灭绝</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-north-atlantic-right-whale-population-has-shrunk-raising-concerns-about-the-future-of-the-critically-endangered-species-180989896/</guid></item><item><title>现代法医调查揭示了在北爱尔兰沼泽中发现的 2000 年前尸体的死因</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-modern-forensic-investigation-reveals-the-cause-of-death-of-a-2000-year-old-body-found-in-an-bog-in-northern-ireland-180989898/</link><description>考古学家与验尸官合作确定，“Ballymacoms More Woman”在似乎是铁器时代的祭祀仪式中被斩首时只有 15 至 22 岁</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:36:20 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-modern-forensic-investigation-reveals-the-cause-of-death-of-a-2000-year-old-body-found-in-an-bog-in-northern-ireland-180989898/</guid></item><item><title>从尼安德特人遗传的基因变异可能会影响现代人类的大脑大小并提供预防精神分裂症的保护</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-gene-variant-inherited-from-neanderthals-might-affect-modern-humans-brain-size-and-provide-protection-against-schizophrenia-180989893/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，当今世界上大约 20% 的欧洲血统的人至少携带一个该变体的副本。它与较小的枕叶（处理视觉信息的区域）有关，并且可使患精神分裂症的风险降低近 10%</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:57:10 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-gene-variant-inherited-from-neanderthals-might-affect-modern-humans-brain-size-and-provide-protection-against-schizophrenia-180989893/</guid></item><item><title>中世纪的读者将洪水、瘟疫和彗星视为末日的预兆，因此他们创作了一本神秘的世界末日艺术品手稿以供随意阅读</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/medieval-readers-saw-floods-plagues-and-comets-as-omens-of-doom-so-they-created-a-mysterious-manuscript-of-apocalyptic-artworks-to-peruse-at-will-180989891/</link><description>《奇迹之书》是一本可能创作于奥格斯堡的 16 世纪手稿，即将拍卖。它有 167 幅描绘极端天气事件和奇怪天象的画作</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:53:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/medieval-readers-saw-floods-plagues-and-comets-as-omens-of-doom-so-they-created-a-mysterious-manuscript-of-apocalyptic-artworks-to-peruse-at-will-180989891/</guid></item><item><title>就在这幅弗里达·卡罗 (Frida Kahlo) 的画作有望以 350 万美元的价格售出之前几个小时，它就被从拍卖会上拍了下来</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/hours-before-it-was-expected-to-sell-for-up-to-3-million-this-frida-kahlo-painting-was-whisked-from-the-auction-block-180989890/</link><description>据称，这幅 1952 年的画作“Congreso de los pueblos por la paz”在可疑的情况下从卡罗位于墨西哥城的博物馆中消失了。遗产组织认为它理应属于墨西哥公众</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:30:48 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/hours-before-it-was-expected-to-sell-for-up-to-3-million-this-frida-kahlo-painting-was-whisked-from-the-auction-block-180989890/</guid></item><item><title>观看欧洲欧几里得太空望远镜捕捉到的令人惊叹的宇宙图像，该望远镜正在绘制最大的 3D 宇宙地图</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-stunning-images-of-the-universe-captured-by-europes-euclid-space-telescope-which-is-buildling-the-biggest-3d-map-of-the-cosmos-180989884/</link><description>这 170 万 GB 的数据包括超过 9 亿个星系、超过 6000 万个潜在类星体以及大约 15,000 个难以捉摸的宇宙现象的候选者，该现象可以帮助科学家了解暗物质和暗能量</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:32:47 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-stunning-images-of-the-universe-captured-by-europes-euclid-space-telescope-which-is-buildling-the-biggest-3d-map-of-the-cosmos-180989884/</guid></item><item><title>吉娃娃似乎带有一点土狼的 DNA，但这可能不是它们拥有无所畏惧的性格的原因</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/chihuahuas-seem-to-carry-a-tiny-bit-of-coyote-dna-but-thats-probably-not-why-they-have-fearless-personalities-180989886/</link><description>新研究表明，郊狼 DNA 约占吉娃娃基因组的 0.1%，这可能是很久以前郊狼与家养狗祖先杂交的结果</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/chihuahuas-seem-to-carry-a-tiny-bit-of-coyote-dna-but-thats-probably-not-why-they-have-fearless-personalities-180989886/</guid></item><item><title>这个人来自丹麦的一个小岛，经历了 6000 年前从狩猎采集到农耕的转变</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/from-a-small-island-in-denmark-this-man-lived-through-the-transition-from-hunter-gathering-to-farming-6000-years-ago-180989889/</link><description>对罗达尔斯人的一项新分析表明，他在一生中目睹了新石器时代革命，在成长过程中主要吃海鲜，然后在成年后转向更多的陆地食物（可能是养殖食物）</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:15:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/from-a-small-island-in-denmark-this-man-lived-through-the-transition-from-hunter-gathering-to-farming-6000-years-ago-180989889/</guid></item><item><title>这种微小、不起眼的真菌是一种“黑暗魔法蘑菇”——第一个被发现含有迷幻化合物和致命毒素的蘑菇</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-tiny-unassuming-fungus-is-a-dark-magic-mushroom-the-first-found-to-contain-both-psychedelic-compounds-and-deadly-toxins-180989885/</link><description>研究人员从佛罗里达州中部湿地长满青苔的棕榈树干中采集了这种蘑菇。众所周知，它的亲戚会产生鹅膏毒素，但这种真菌在处理时却令人惊讶地变成蓝色，这是该生物体产生裸盖菇素的明显迹象</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:06:13 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-tiny-unassuming-fungus-is-a-dark-magic-mushroom-the-first-found-to-contain-both-psychedelic-compounds-and-deadly-toxins-180989885/</guid></item><item><title>古埃及的圣猫是如何生活的？ 100多具被拆开的木乃伊揭示了其恶劣的生活条件、感染和生前的暴力行为</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/how-did-ancient-egypts-sacred-cats-live-more-than-100-unwrapped-mummies-reveal-poor-living-conditions-infections-and-violence-before-death-180989888/</link><description>对 131 件博物馆标本进行的骨学和化学测试显示，后来被制成木乃伊的家猫和野生捕获的丛林猫患病率和身体创伤率很高</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:58:18 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/how-did-ancient-egypts-sacred-cats-live-more-than-100-unwrapped-mummies-reveal-poor-living-conditions-infections-and-violence-before-death-180989888/</guid></item><item><title>近 600 年来，这幅神秘的扬·凡·艾克 (Jan van Eyck) 画作一直让观众着迷。这真的是一幅乔装的自画像吗？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-almost-600-years-this-enigmatic-jan-van-eyck-painting-has-entraced-viewers-could-it-actually-be-a-self-portrait-in-disguise-180989883/</link><description>关于“阿尔诺菲尼肖像”的新理论诞生之​​际，伦敦国家美术馆首次汇集了该艺术家所有 10 幅已知肖像画</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:32:16 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-almost-600-years-this-enigmatic-jan-van-eyck-painting-has-entraced-viewers-could-it-actually-be-a-self-portrait-in-disguise-180989883/</guid></item><item><title>SpaceX 首次捕捉到其星际飞船的上级，使该公司距离可重复使用火箭又近了一步</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/spacex-catches-the-upper-stage-of-its-starship-for-the-first-time-making-the-company-one-step-closer-to-a-reusable-rocket-180989877/</link><description>绕地球 14 圈后，星舰的上部下降到地球表面，并被一对巨大的筷子状机械臂抓住。然而，该公司未能抢占其先前展示过的下层舞台</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/spacex-catches-the-upper-stage-of-its-starship-for-the-first-time-making-the-company-one-step-closer-to-a-reusable-rocket-180989877/</guid></item><item><title>美国已经失去了维持了 26 年的麻疹消除地位。案件现已激增至数十年来的最高水平</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-us-has-lost-its-measles-elimination-status-which-its-held-for-26-years-cases-have-now-surged-to-the-highest-levels-in-decades-180989878/</link><description>今年迄今为止，疾病控制与预防中心已确认超过 5,400 例麻疹病例（这是自 1991 年以来的最高年度病例总数），并爆发了 43 起麻疹疫情。疫苗接种率下降可能是罪魁祸首</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-us-has-lost-its-measles-elimination-status-which-its-held-for-26-years-cases-have-now-surged-to-the-highest-levels-in-decades-180989878/</guid></item></channel></rss>